1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:01,870
Ladies and gentlemen,

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,500
Amtrak is happy to announce our arrival in New York City.

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,540
The train will be stopping in five minutes.

4
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:07,100
Please check to be sure you have your belongings.

5
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,130
And have a good stay in the Big Apple.

6
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:10,330
Thank you.

7
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:12,550
Well, here we are.

8
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,370
It was so nice meeting you, Mr.Stewart.

9
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:18,350
And nice meeting you, too, Mrs.Tobin.

10
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,800
Please look us up.

11
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,070
We're in the phone book.

12
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:24,060
Dr. Philip Stewart, in Riverdale.

13
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:25,080
Your son?

14
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:30,160
That's right. And have a good time in New York.

15
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,590
And don't be so independent.

16
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:47,980
You're very lucky to have a caring family.

17
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:49,290
When can we go fishing?

18
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:52,650
Robbie, we'll go fishing soon,

19
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:54,550
and we'll take your dad with us.

20
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:58,380
I'm ready, Grandpa. You name the day.

21
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,130
That's a great idea, Grandpa!

22
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:02,350
Philip needs a day off.

23
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:04,360
Let's give him our presents--now.

24
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:05,750
Good idea.

25
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:11,320
Presents--for me?

26
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:13,650
From me and Marilyn.

27
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,620
And this one's from me.

28
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:33,650
I looked all over the house to find it.

29
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:43,760
Richard, these are terrific pictures.

30
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:49,150
This one really brings back memories.

31
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,680
You remember that day, Robbie?

32
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:57,010
I sure do. It was fun.

33
00:01:57,010 --> 00:02:04,420
Oh, I'm sorry Susan isn't here.

34
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,850
I miss her very much.

35
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:09,180
She feels bad, too, Grandpa.

36
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,240
She called to say the plane was delayed.

37
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,110
You know airports.

38
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:15,960
I can't wait to see her.

39
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:21,900
She looks just like Grandma at that age.

40
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,870
I'd better unpack.

41
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:30,540
I started traveling twenty-four hours ago.

42
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:34,010
I'm not so young anymore.

43
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,580
Don't you want something to eat?

44
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:37,700
No, thanks.

45
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:41,000
After a good night's sleep, I'll enjoy breakfast even more.

46
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,450
Well, come on, Dad.

47
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:44,440
Ellen and I'll take you to your room.

48
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,490
I'm sure glad you're here, Grandpa.

49
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:47,550
Good night, Grandpa.

50
00:02:47,550 --> 00:03:04,240
Pleasant dreams.

51
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:08,010
Philip, do you have the key to the trunk?

52
00:03:08,010 --> 00:03:17,160
I have the key, but it doesn't work.

53
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:31,620
I sent the wrong key.

54
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:37,820
I have something for you. I made it myself.

55
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:40,930
I think you'll enjoy it.

56
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:44,020
I researched it for over a year.

57
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:49,520
It's our family tree.

58
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:53,800
Oh, Grandpa! How exciting!

59
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,310
Fabulous!

60
00:03:55,310 --> 00:04:00,100
Why, I didn't know that your grandfather was born in Germany.

61
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,780
Lots of interesting information about our family.

62
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:06,490
A gift from me.

63
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:09,000
Thank you so much.

64
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,150
Grandpa! Grandpa!

65
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:15,800
Oh, Grandpa, I'm so happy to see you!

66
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:21,810
Oh, you look so beautiful, Susan. My granddaughter.

67
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:27,020
Like I always said, you look just like Grandma.

68
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:31,300
I think you're going to be very happy here with us.

69
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,950
I know you will.

70
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:36,950
I don't feel alone anymore.
